#d	Khmer words by English word: every Khmer word or phrase that corresponds to it, commonest first, and the Greek and Hebrew words the Bible translates by it (Strong’s numbers: STEPBible’s tagging of the BSB, CC BY 4.0); by sense where the Chinese Bible tells them apart (the Chinese Union Version: the Khmer words the same English word goes with in the same verses, by the Chinese it goes with there; a sense a Chinese word, with its meanings from CC-CEDICT and Wiktionary, CC BY-SA 4.0). Machine-made by word-aligning 7 Khmer Bibles with 8 English ones, and Khmer–English sentence pairs from <a href="https://opus.nlpl.eu/">OPUS</a> (subtitles, web pages, KDE and translatewiki software strings, Wikipedia names and pages, TICO-19, Global Voices, TED talks, Tatoeba, NLLB, ALT) and FLORES-200, with eflomal. People’s translations too: English Wiktionary’s translation tables, the English glosses of Wiktionary’s Khmer entries (via Kaikki) and the SBBIC English–Khmer dictionary’s (GPL 2); a machine-aligned Khmer word only where one of these gives it, a Khmer dictionary has it (Headley’s and Chuon Nath’s, only to check by), or a good share of the sentences do. With another language’s on, a dictionary between them. (Archaic): English only the KJV and ASV have; a corpus’s name after a word only it has. Unchecked: verify before relying on it.
